# 286. Walls and Gates

- **LeetCode:** https://leetcode.com/problems/walls-and-gates/
- **Topic:** Graph, Matrix, Multi-Source BFS
- **Language:** Java
- **Status:** Approach understood

## 1. My Intuition

This problem follows the same Multi-Source BFS pattern.

We need to find the distance of every empty room from its nearest gate.

Instead of creating a new matrix, we can modify the existing matrix itself.

## 2. My Approach

1. Traverse the matrix and add all gates (0) to the queue.
2. Start BFS from all gates simultaneously.
3. Explore all four directions.
4. If a neighboring cell contains Integer.MAX_VALUE:
   - Update its value to the current cell's value + 1.
   - Add it to the queue.
5. Leave walls (-1) undisturbed.
6. Ignore already visited cells.
7. If an empty room cannot be reached from any gate, it remains INF.

## 3. Where I Got Stuck / My Mistake

No major difficulty.

The key observation was that an additional distance matrix is unnecessary because the original matrix can store the distances.

## 4. What Clicked

The same Multi-Source BFS algorithm can be applied without creating a separate distance matrix.

The condition:

rooms[nr][nc] == Integer.MAX_VALUE

ensures that only unvisited empty rooms are processed.

Unreachable rooms automatically retain their original value.

## 5. Final Submitted Code

class Solution {
    public void wallsAndGates(int[][] rooms) {
        int m = rooms.length;
        int n = rooms[0].length;

        Queue<int[]> q = new LinkedList<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                if (rooms[i][j] == 0) {
                    q.offer(new int[]{i, j});
                }
            }
        }

        int[] dr = {-1, 1, 0, 0};
        int[] dc = {0, 0, -1, 1};

        while (!q.isEmpty()) {
            int[] curr = q.poll();
            int r = curr[0];
            int c = curr[1];

            for (int k = 0; k < 4; k++) {
                int nr = r + dr[k];
                int nc = c + dc[k];

                if (nr >= 0 && nr < m &&
                    nc >= 0 && nc < n &&
                    rooms[nr][nc] == Integer.MAX_VALUE) {

                    rooms[nr][nc] = rooms[r][c] + 1;
                    q.offer(new int[]{nr, nc});
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

## 6. Complexity Analysis

- Time Complexity: O(m * n)
- Auxiliary Space Complexity: O(m * n)

## 7. Revision Notes

- All gates are initial sources.
- Use the existing matrix to store distances.
- Integer.MAX_VALUE represents an unvisited empty room.
- Walls are never visited.
- Unreachable rooms remain unchanged.
- BFS finds the nearest gate.
